# Anvilhead (Fabric, Minecraft 1.21.1)

A tall silent stalker. Built from the reference silhouette: huge flat slab head, tiny pale eyes, thin neck.

## Behavior
- **Spawns** (custom spawner, ONE in the whole server at a time, avg. every ~7 min while conditions hold):
  forest at night only (daytime storms don't count), or a dark cave (light level 3 or less). In caves it scans ~80 candidate spots and picks the darkest one it can find that is hidden from the player. Always hidden from the player.
- **Stalks**: stays ~20 blocks away, picks spots hidden from your line of sight, preferably beside a tree trunk
  or in dark cave corners. Silent footsteps; faint heartbeat when close.
- **Looked at**: freezes. Stared at ~4.5 s: vanishes in smoke.
- **Attacks (rare)**: after 45 s alive, roughly 1% per second while you are in low light, not looking, within 26 blocks.
  It rushes at faster-than-sprint speed, hits once (8 dmg + Darkness + Slowness) and disappears.
- Any hit on it while stalking makes it vanish. Leaves after 6 minutes.

## Tuning
Constants at the top of `AnvilheadEntity` (RUSH_ODDS, STARE_LIMIT, MAX_LIFETIME ...) and `AnvilheadSpawner` (SPAWN_ODDS).

## Testing
`/summon anvilhead:anvilhead` or use the spawn egg (Spawn Eggs tab).

## Pitch-black darkness (client mixin)
`LightmapTextureManagerMixin` makes the Overworld pitch black wherever there is no real light source.
The body is lit only by the (now black) lightmap, so it disappears; the eyes use a fullbright layer, so they stay visible.
Tune `DARK_FLOOR` / `FULL_BRIGHT` at the top of the mixin. Night Vision still lets you see.

## Chase cutscene
When it decides to attack (rare roll, you're in low light and not looking), it does NOT just run at you:
1. If it was hiding, it appears 12-20 blocks in front of you with a clear line of sight to its face.
2. **Cutscene (5.5 s):** movement and mouse are locked, the camera whips onto its face and zooms in.
   Heartbeat for 1.5 s, then it ROARS (head thrown back, arms wide, camera shake).
3. **Chase:** controls return, the chase theme (`sounds/chase_theme.ogg`) starts, and it hunts you at ~sprint speed
   for up to 2:37 (the length of the theme). One strike ends it (it vanishes and the music fades out). If it gives up or you get away, same.
Tune: `ChaseSequence` (timings), `AnvilheadEntity.CHASE_SPEED`, `CHASE_TIMEOUT`.
To swap the music: replace `assets/anvilhead/sounds/chase_theme.ogg` (OGG Vorbis).

## Chase screen effects
From the moment the chase starts (not during the cutscene): the camera shakes (rumble + hard jolts, visual only, aim is unaffected)
and an opaque jagged black border with black/white glitch blocks and scanline tears eats into your vision.
Both ramp in over 0.5 s, get stronger the closer it is, and fade out when it vanishes.
Tune in `ChaseOverlay` (border thickness, block counts) and `ChaseClient.shakeOffsets` (shake strength).

## Size and the "peeking" night spawn
- The Anvilhead is now **4 blocks tall** (hitbox 0.8 x 4.0, model scaled to match). It needs 4 blocks of headroom,
  so it can only stand in cave passages that are at least 4 tall.
- **Night / surface:** it only spawns behind the **shortest tree trunk that is at least 5 blocks tall** (scan of the ring 18-40
  blocks around you), just behind it and slightly off-centre so its wide slab head and part of its face poke out past the trunk.
  It never moves; it just turns to face you. Look **directly at its head** (crosshair on the head, clear line of sight,
  ~0.25 s) and it steps out from behind the tree and the cutscene + chase begin. It leaves at dawn, or after 2.5 min
  if you never look at it.
- **Caves:** unchanged (darkest hidden spot, freezes when watched, vanishes if stared at, rare random chase).

## The eyes event (1 in a trillion, every tick)
Every server tick, every Overworld player rolls a **1 in 1,000,000,000,000** chance (`EyeEventManager.ODDS`). If it hits:
1. Eyes (`textures/gui/eye.png`) open on that player's screen **one after another**. The first comes after 2 s, then every ~5 s;
   each gap is 6% shorter than the last (minimum 3 ticks), so it starts slow and speeds up. Each eye has a heartbeat that gets louder.
   50 eyes take about 80 s (`EyeSequence`).
2. After the 50th eye there is a 2 s pause, then a **shockwave**: white-out flash, expanding rings from the centre of the screen
   that wipe the eyes away (eyes just ahead of the ring get shoved outward), FOV snap + camera shake, sonic boom.
3. At that moment an Anvilhead spawns **~50 blocks away, day or night, surface or underground** and the **chase starts immediately**
   (roar + chase theme, no cutscene). Any existing Anvilhead is removed first (still max one). If no valid spot is found
   it retries for 10 s and tapers the distance in (50 -> 40 -> 25 -> 10 blocks).
The event is cancelled if the player dies, leaves the Overworld, or the difficulty is Peaceful. Only one event runs at a time.

**Testing** (op level 2): `/anvilhead eyes` starts the eyes event on you; `/anvilhead chase` skips straight to the 50-block chase spawn.
Tune: `EyeSequence` (timing, 0.94 = speed-up rate), `EyeEventClient` (eye size/layout, shockwave look).
Note: the shockwave is drawn as a HUD overlay (rings, flash, FOV kick, shake), not a true refraction shader.

